From 20a54601f8b8a2b066547ac2763ceedcd8f937e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Duprey <509630+destinal@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 13:52:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 09/19] Claude Code plugin: show OSC 7501 program status

Konsole now answers the Program Status Protocol's feature query, so
Claude Code reports its own state: working, blocked on a permission or a
question, done, and idle, including when the user interrupts a turn,
which runs no hook. The plugin keeps the reports as records, one per id,
and shows the most urgent through the session status it shares with the
hooks and OSC 21337, whichever wrote last. A port of iTerm2's
ProgramStatusRecords and the status half of its ProgramStatusController:

- a report replaces its record; clear removes a record and its
  descendants, or every record; past 256 the oldest is evicted;
- blocked, error, done, working, idle, in that order of urgency, the
  most recent winning ties, with app inherited from an ancestor;
- a new prompt ends working, blocked and idle records, a key press turns
  done and error idle, a full reset or the program exiting removes all;
- the status uses cc-status's words and colors, and the detail is the
  message, the kind of block, or a child record's title.

With Claude Code reporting interrupts itself, sessions no longer need to
pass as ConEmu to get OSC 9;4 progress from it, so that is removed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
